  ('e69875f8-f41d-5170-b329-b62bbd070197', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which quotation best explains why experts suggest leaving feeders up after the last bird is seen?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"In the weeks before it leaves, it may nearly double its weight.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"A late traveler passing through may still need a meal.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Many believe the birds are born with a sense of direction.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"Flowers such as bee balm and trumpet vine give them nectar.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"A late traveler passing through may still need a meal."$q$, $q$The sentence right after the advice gives the reason: a late bird may still pass by and need food. The flower sentence tells another way to feed birds, but not why feeders should stay up longer.$q$, 'draft', '31eed681-81aa-5f68-b72d-83a9486dcc88')
