  ('78111ee0-18b1-5fec-b649-af3f67252236', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which two details from the passage together best support the idea that migration is risky for a hummingbird?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It may fly about five hundred miles over open water, and a bird that is too thin may not finish.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It weighs about as much as a paper clip, and people hang feeders filled with sugar water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Scientists are still studying its sense of direction, and experts suggest feeders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It travels alone instead of in a flock, and bee balm and trumpet vine give it nectar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It may fly about five hundred miles over open water, and a bird that is too thin may not finish.$q$, $q$A long flight over water with no place to stop, plus the warning that a thin bird "may not have enough energy to finish," both point to danger. Feeders and flowers are ways people help, not signs of risk.$q$, 'draft', '31eed681-81aa-5f68-b72d-83a9486dcc88')
