   $q$What can the reader infer about why some towns asked families to save every scrap of cloth?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Families were not allowed to wear old shirts made of cotton.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Papermakers needed rags, and there were not always enough of them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Towns wanted to sell the cloth to people who made wood paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Cloth scraps were used to build the frames for the screens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Papermakers needed rags, and there were not always enough of them.$q$, $q$The passage says rags were the main ingredient and paper "was often hard to get," so saving cloth helped supply the papermakers. Nothing in the passage connects the cloth to wood paper or to the frames.$q$, 'draft', '6a6d670c-33e5-5154-9a57-ce09c9a1e33e')
