   $q$Which quotation best supports the author's claim that a weather station would not be expensive?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"A sign-up chart would make sure someone checks the station every school day.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"\"Our school has a science lab, a row of tomato plants and a fish tank.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"Students can even build the rain gauge from a clear plastic bottle and a ruler.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"They would record numbers every morning and look for patterns over the season.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Students can even build the rain gauge from a clear plastic bottle and a ruler."$q$, $q$Building a rain gauge from a bottle and a ruler shows the parts can be cheap. The sentence about recording numbers supports a different claim, that the station would make science into real research.$q$, 'draft', '785b7f77-91f6-5664-a58c-da3bfae33c0a')
