   $q$What can the reader infer about how the author compares reading a textbook with measuring weather?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author thinks textbooks are better because their numbers are always correct.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-claim"},{"text":"The author thinks measuring weather yourself teaches more than only reading about it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author thinks students should stop using science textbooks for the whole year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The author thinks reading and measuring teach exactly the same lessons to students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author thinks measuring weather yourself teaches more than only reading about it.$q$, $q$The author says a station would "turn science class into real research" and help students "think like scientists," so measuring is seen as better. The author never says to stop using textbooks completely, so that choice goes too far.$q$, 'draft', '785b7f77-91f6-5664-a58c-da3bfae33c0a')
