   $q$According to the passage, how do puppet makers show small details in a puppet's shadow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They attach extra rods to the puppet's arms and legs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-purpose"},{"text":"They punch tiny holes in patterns across the figure.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They paint the details on the screen with bright colors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They move the puppet closer to the light behind it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They punch tiny holes in patterns across the figure.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says light passing through tiny holes shows "details like the lace on a dress." Moving a puppet closer to the light makes the shadow "blurrier," which would hide details.$q$, 'draft', 'fbb1ed0c-1000-55b4-aff4-3ce4455a0460')
