   $q$A student writes, "Shadow puppets can only make plain black shadows." Which quotation best shows that this statement is not accurate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Some puppets are colored and partly see-through, so their shadows glow in soft shades of red, green and gold.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"A light shines on a screen, and puppets held behind the screen cast shadows the audience can see.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"When light passes through the holes, the shadow shows details like the lace on a dress or the feathers on a bird.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"\"When a puppet moves closer to the light, its shadow grows larger and blurrier.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Some puppets are colored and partly see-through, so their shadows glow in soft shades of red, green and gold."$q$, $q$Shadows that "glow in soft shades of red, green and gold" are not plain black. The sentence about holes shows detail in the shadow, but it does not say anything about color.$q$, 'draft', 'fbb1ed0c-1000-55b4-aff4-3ce4455a0460')
